# Conventional Commits

Every commit in a XingAI repo must follow the conventional commit format. This is enforced in CI and enables automated changelogs.

## Format

```
<type>(<scope>): <short summary>

[optional body]

[optional footer]
```

## Types

| Type | When to use |
|---|---|
| `feat` | New user-facing feature or capability |
| `fix` | Bug fix |
| `refactor` | Code change with no behavior change |
| `perf` | Performance improvement |
| `test` | Adding or fixing tests |
| `docs` | Documentation only |
| `chore` | Build, deps, config, tooling — no src change |
| `ci` | GitHub Actions or CI config |
| `style` | Formatting, whitespace — no logic change |
| `revert` | Reverts a prior commit |

## Scope (optional)

Use the feature area or module name: `worker`, `ui`, `auth`, `i18n`, `api`, `cache`, `agent`.

## Examples

```
feat(worker): add stale cache refresh with background requeue
fix(ui): correct bottom nav overlap on iPhone SE
refactor(agent): split orchestrator plan step into separate function
test(api): add integration tests for /demo/run endpoint
chore(deps): bump next from 14.1.0 to 15.0.0
ci: add npm audit step to PR workflow
docs(adr): add ADR-003 for cache TTL decision
```

## Rules

- Summary line: 72 characters max, lowercase, no period at end.
- Use imperative mood: "add", "fix", "remove" — not "added", "fixed", "removed".
- Breaking changes: add `!` after type/scope and a `BREAKING CHANGE:` footer.
- Do not use vague summaries: "updates", "changes", "fixes stuff", "WIP".

## Breaking Change Format

```
feat(api)!: rename /demo/run to /api/v1/run

BREAKING CHANGE: all clients must update the endpoint path.
```

## What This Enables

- Automated `CHANGELOG.md` generation with `conventional-changelog` or `release-please`
- Semantic version bumps (`feat` → minor, `fix` → patch, `!` → major)
- Clear git history that non-authors can read
- CI can block merges on non-conforming commit messages via `commitlint`

## commitlint Setup (add to new projects)

```bash
npm install --save-dev @commitlint/cli @commitlint/config-conventional
```

```js
// commitlint.config.js
export default { extends: ['@commitlint/config-conventional'] };
```

```yaml
# .github/workflows/commitlint.yml
- uses: wagoid/commitlint-github-action@v6
```
